{"author":{"id":"a66e0db0201c515c5090d5e52c036411dda9ba2f138110a926616a18a8ea0dd6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790677520,"nonce":"sIdAXT484jU9lA+6DG0AHJqSq1s=","title":"Share one GPU implementation across Caribou, Ash and Rayzor","message":"Caribou's cb_gpu plugin contains the most complete wgpu surface, but its API declaration, WebGPU IDL, generator, resource tables and backend all live in the Caribou repository. Ash and Rayzor would otherwise have to copy the catalog and maintain handwritten Haxe externs.\n\nMove the canonical API and IDL to xgpu. Generate Caribou bindings, HashLink/Ash externs and Rayzor externs from that source, including runtime-specific Future\u003cT\u003e names for WebIDL Promise\u003cT\u003e. Keep GPU objects behind the same generational Rust handles so runtime adapters only translate text, shared bytes, errors, roots and asynchronous completion.\n\nThe first extraction should make Caribou consume xgpu without losing native, browser-wire or fixture coverage. The existing full backend can live in the Caribou adapter while its resource table moves into the neutral core. Subsequent Ash and Rayzor adapters should generate both their native export tables and Haxe externs; they must not introduce another API list.\n\nRuntime prerequisites:\n\n- Ash needs an externally completable Future\u003cT\u003e ABI; tracked in Ash as df8fe0662a135853b1d2c21f87dc86d38f6bb3955814bc279b39d9ee372854d5.\n- Rayzor has rayzor.concurrent.Future\u003cT\u003e, but its public constructor is lazy-closure based. Its xgpu adapter needs a native pending/completion entry point for wgpu callbacks.\n- Buffers must remain borrowed/shared at calls and rooted only when a descriptor retains them.\n\nAcceptance:\n\n- one canonical gpu.api.rs and WebGPU/canvas IDL live in xgpu;\n- xgpu owns the WebIDL/wire generator and emits conventional Haxe externs for Ash and Rayzor;\n- native features come from the same pinned wgpu-types version for every emitter;\n- Caribou's GPU package builds and fixtures run while sourcing its generator, backend and API from xgpu;\n- Ash and Rayzor native adapter generation is completed once their externally completable future seams exist.","files":null}]}